#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:9
msgid "Launching multiple nodes - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:11
msgid ""
"A launch file lets you start multiple nodes simultaneously with a single "
"command, without opening a separate terminal for each. This article shows "
"you how to run an existing launch file with ``ros2 launch``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:14
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: how-to | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:18
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:21
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:23
msgid ""
"Use ``ros2 launch <package> <launch_file>`` to run multiple nodes at once "
"from a single launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:25
msgid ""
"You can run a launch file that already comes with a package, or create a new "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:27
msgid ""
"To learn how to write your own launch file, see :doc:`Creating a launch file "
"<../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:30
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:33
msgid ""
"Source ROS in every new terminal you open. See :doc:`Configuring environment "
"<../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:37
msgid "1 Run a launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:39
msgid "To run a launch file, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:41
msgid "$ ros2 launch <package_name> <launch_file_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:45
msgid ""
"For example, to run the ``multisim.launch.py`` file, which is included in "
"the ``turtlesim`` package, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:47
msgid "$ ros2 launch turtlesim multisim.launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:51
msgid ""
"You do not need to create this file yourself. It is installed with "
"``turtlesim``, so any machine with that package can run this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:54
msgid "This runs the following launch file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:56
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"import launch_ros.actions\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim1', package='turtlesim',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node', output='screen'),\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim2', package='turtlesim',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node', output='screen'),\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:61
msgid ""
"The ``multisim.launch.py`` launch file is written in Python, but you can "
"also use XML and YAML to create launch files. You can see a comparison of "
"these different launch formats in :doc:`../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/"
"Launch-file-different-formats`."
msgstr ""

