#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:78
msgid "Can I write a launch file in a language other than Python?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:79
msgid ""
"Yes. ROS supports launch files written in Python, XML, and YAML. For a "
"comparison of these formats, see :doc:`../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/"
"Launch-file-different-formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:83
msgid "How do I write my own launch file?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:84
msgid ""
"See :doc:`Creating a launch file <../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/"
"Creating-Launch-Files>` for a step-by-step guide. The :doc:`ROS launch "
"tutorials <../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-Main>` index lists "
"further launch topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:87
msgid "Can I pass arguments to a launch file?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:88
msgid ""
"Yes. Use ``ros2 launch <package> <launch_file> <arg>:=<value>`` to pass "
"arguments at the command line. Arguments must be declared within the launch "
"file itself."
msgstr ""
